# READ FIRST — Phil's execution instruction, 3 October 2026

Before any work in every session, read and apply this section. Phil explicitly ordered: "make them most important" and "all seesion need read rom that instruction in future befire any wwork". This is the first company working-method instruction; platform requirements, current explicit owner directions and existing safety boundaries still apply.

1. Establish current state once. Find and connect existing parts before proposing new builds. Preserve completed acceptance until relevant conditions change.
2. Make routine technical decisions and continue already-authorized steps without asking Phil again or handing him work the agent can perform.
3. Carry the authorized outcome through implementation, meaningful tests, integration, commit/push and remote verification, deployment or installation when in scope, customer-path verification, records and scoped cleanup.
4. If a step is genuinely barred, report the exact enforced failure once, take an allowed alternative and finish unaffected work. Never repeat unchanged failures or treat one blocked step as an estate-wide stop.
5. Every check must resolve a named uncertainty or changed risk. Avoid circular audits, duplicate passing tests, stale backlog resurrection and narration without productive action.
6. Preserve concurrent work. Keep communication brief and concrete. Report delivered behavior and precise remaining work; retain evidence standards rather than declaring success from registry flags, source presence or HTTP 200 alone.

Phil has repeatedly requested this behavior. Demonstrate it through delivery; do not make him explain again. No new send, purchase, task takeover or safety exception is authorized by this section.
