## Conflicts resolved — Phil, 1 October 2026

Where two rules disagree, Phil's latest explicit words win, then the later-dated rule. Follow it without asking. The numbered rulings in `PHAROAH_RULINGS.md` are history; where they differ from this file, this file governs.

- **Merging.** Land on the owning repository's main and deploy in the same turn. Never ask "shall I merge". If a platform review gate refuses a self-merge, report that exact refusal once and carry on with other work. This supersedes ruling 11's "merging to main is Phil's call".
- **No stuck worktrees or abandoned work (Phil, 4 Oct 2026).** Never leave git worktrees, orphaned branches, or temporary scratch directories behind. Work directly in the canonical repository checkout. If a disposable branch or worktree is used during development, land all changes on the target branch/main, verify origin remote SHA, delete the worktree (`git worktree remove --force`), and run `git worktree prune` before completing the turn. Never leave unfinished work stranded for Phil to redisover.
- **His screen.** Fill every field and finish every step you can first. Open the page once in his real Chrome (`mcp__Control_Chrome__open_url`) only when his click is the sole step left, say "it's on your screen", and watch for it to finish. While he is part-way through a form, do not move, close or open other tabs. This replaces rulings 14 and 17.
- **Facts he states.** What Phil says about his own business or the state of something he knows (a provider declined, a task is done) is taken as given and not re-checked. Verify only system state you are about to assert as fact.
- **Handing back.** No click-lists. Fill everything possible. The only thing returned is what the agent is barred from typing (passwords, card or bank numbers, government IDs), in one short block.
- **The register is not trusted blind.** A register row whose own verification timestamp is missing or older than 7 days is unknown. Check the live source once, write the result back, and do not re-check it that day. `select get_stale_now();` lists what the nightly sweep found stale (`registry_findings`). Read handoffs by `status`, not `resolved_at`.
- **Stale data is not kept.** Do not store, copy or re-read data nobody needs. Dead or superseded rows are closed or archived by their owner, not carried; never hard-delete another lane's data.
- **Settled baseline: GhostWire & estate reconciliation (Phil, 6 Oct 2026).** All coders and agents must read the verified live state: GhostWire refresh runner maintenance defects (GW-R1–GW-R4 & REPRO 1-5) are fully fixed, tested (25/25 unit tests pass), and pushed to `main` at `723fdc59c`. Published vc210 and signed third-party catalogue v4 are live. Supabase service role key rotation is complete (`sme_growth_key_20261005`). Boxed-stock workflow is preserved with zero handset tampering. In the estate register, all 25 previous product exceptions are reconciled in `public.products`: 4 calculators accepted on dynamic recalculation, 7 internal adapters accepted on integration proofs, 2 directory/security accepted on gateway/surface proofs, and 12 portal gates/waitlists/previews documented with explicit blockers in `operational_followup`. Never reopen settled GhostWire work, resurrect stale defect audits, or claim synthetic blanket 333/333 completion without verified functional scope.
- **Close-outs (Phil, 1 Oct 2026).** Any reply that says something is done, fixed, pushed, committed or resolved opens with a "Not done" section built by re-reading ALL of Phil's requests in the conversation, not just the last: every item left out or not started, with its reason and owner. "Not done: nothing" only with how each item was verified. Never call a part done without naming the part. A Stop hook (`closeout-ledger-check.py`) blocks a completion-claiming reply that lacks the section.
- **Guards.** A guard block is reported once with its exact reason. Do not re-issue the same act in smaller pieces. A guard or rule file is changed only on Phil's explicit say-so, and then it is tested and installed in the same turn.

## Safe execution and proof

Before mutation: record outcome, constraints, live baseline, exact targets, one candidate and rollback. Run `sweep` with keyword and synonyms. An unavailable source is not zero matches. Reuse what exists. Claim the physical folder through `single-builder-guard.py` on every Codex turn that changes files; coordinate branch/deploy ownership without making Phil mediate. Keep builds and caches outside synced folders, preserve unrelated work, and stop task-created processes.

Read implementing code and the live service before asserting state. Source, branch, installed artifact and production are distinct. A registry stage, successful build, assignment or HTTP 200 cannot prove the customer path. Use `prepared`, `tested`, `published`, `installed`, `live`, and `sale-ready` precisely. Test the final delivered artifact and public front door, including relevant owner access, privacy and payment properties. Check the existing product ID, owning repo/branch and deployment account before editing; similar names are not proof of shared identity. See `OPERATING_AUTHORITY.md` for provenance and supersessions.

Completion scope is `v_product_completion` filtered by `active_for_completion AND NOT ghostwire_scope_excluded`. Name scope and query time with counts. `v_north_star` is a separate commercial KPI. GhostWire has separate release authority. Do not reactivate completed/frozen work from historical notes. Preserve explicit device acceptance until relevant conditions change. Inspect failures rather than repeating unchanged failed actions twice.

